<%# locals: (content: nil, url: nil, method: nil, label: nil, **attrs) %>
<%#
  Board: columns of cards, dragged between columns and up and down one (the runeui--board
  Stimulus controller). The block is its ui :board_column's, each holding ui :board_card's.

    ui :board, url: move_tasks_path, label: "Tasks by status" do
      ui :board_column, id: "planned", title: "Planned" do
        ui :board_card, id: task.id, title: task.title, href: task_path(task), meta: "Due Friday"
      end
    end

  A move shows at once and sends one request: PATCH (method:) to the card's url:, else its
  column's, else the board's, with card (the card's id), column (the column's id) and before
  (the id of the card it now sits before, blank at the end). Answer with Turbo Streams, or
  nothing (head :no_content); answer with an error and the card goes back, with a toast.

    def move
      task = Task.find(params[:card])
      task.move!(status: params[:column], before: params[:before].presence)
      head :no_content
    end

  Keys: the arrows go from card to card, Shift with an arrow moves the card you're on (each
  move is read out), Enter opens it. On a touch screen, press and hold a card to pick it up.
  Cards a stream adds (turbo_stream.append "board-list-planned") or a morph brings just work.
%>
<%= ui_tag(:div, { role: "group", aria: { label: (label || "Board") }, data: { slot: "board", controller: "runeui--board", runeui__board_url_value: url, runeui__board_method_value: method&.to_s } }, attrs) do %>
  <%= content %>
  <div class="ui-sr-only" aria-live="assertive" data-runeui--board-target="status"></div>
<% end %>
